1
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:07,240
I want Mariko to be happy.

2
00:00:08,308 --> 00:00:09,275
But…

3
00:00:09,342 --> 00:00:14,881
You have been continually committing
criminal acts all this time.

4
00:00:15,382 --> 00:00:17,751
I was wrong the whole time.

5
00:00:17,817 --> 00:00:21,354
Don't you decide what my happiness is!

6
00:00:21,421 --> 00:00:24,324
Me disappearing is what's best for Mariko.

7
00:00:25,191 --> 00:00:28,094
That's how I can protect
Mariko's happiness.

8
00:00:41,341 --> 00:00:43,343
‎BEST FOR MARIKO

9
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:44,244
Doing things on your own

10
00:00:44,844 --> 00:00:47,480
without my knowledge,
claiming it was for me?

11
00:00:48,214 --> 00:00:50,750
That's just creepy! All of it is creepy!

12
00:00:51,518 --> 00:00:54,487
Doing things without Mariko's knowledge

13
00:00:55,488 --> 00:00:56,656
is bad.

14
00:01:00,293 --> 00:01:02,429
If you leave my side,
I will never forgive you!

15
00:01:03,263 --> 00:01:06,299
I will never forgive you.

16
00:01:06,866 --> 00:01:09,169
Leaving Mariko's side

17
00:01:10,470 --> 00:01:11,304
is bad.

18
00:01:13,907 --> 00:01:16,009
BAD

19
00:01:16,776 --> 00:01:21,081
What am I supposed to do
for Mariko from now on?

20
00:01:24,150 --> 00:01:25,218
MARIKO

21
00:01:25,285 --> 00:01:26,152
POST

22
00:01:28,088 --> 00:01:29,956
COMMENTS

23
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:36,463
Up until now, I would have gathered
information on this person

24
00:01:36,529 --> 00:01:40,433
and observed whether they were a risk
factor threatening Mariko's smile, but…

25
00:01:41,568 --> 00:01:44,704
What you are doing is stalking.

26
00:01:49,909 --> 00:01:52,278
I LIKE GOING TO CAFES

27
00:01:52,345 --> 00:01:53,947
MARIKO 08

28
00:01:54,013 --> 00:01:55,582
UNFOLLOW

29
00:01:58,017 --> 00:01:59,252
UNFOLLOW

30
00:01:59,319 --> 00:02:00,887
FOLLOW

31
00:02:02,722 --> 00:02:05,358
This isn't my job anymore.

32
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:15,168
Yukimura…

33
00:02:17,170 --> 00:02:18,338
I'm sorry.

34
00:02:18,404 --> 00:02:19,539
Yukimura!

35
00:02:20,206 --> 00:02:21,341
Sota Yukimura.

36
00:02:23,076 --> 00:02:25,245
The boy you're looking for

37
00:02:26,546 --> 00:02:27,680
is at our company.

38
00:02:27,747 --> 00:02:29,149
His name is Sota Yukimura.

39
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:40,793
It's the darkest
under the street lamp, huh?

40
00:02:43,429 --> 00:02:46,766
So they're childhood friends
and coworkers?

41
00:02:46,833 --> 00:02:48,101
What the hell?

42
00:02:48,635 --> 00:02:51,437
If that's the case, you should have
just told me from the start.

43
00:03:46,059 --> 00:03:49,128
-Let me go! Help me!
-Somebody!

44
00:03:49,195 --> 00:03:51,197
Somebody, please come!

45
00:03:55,835 --> 00:03:58,838
THE SERIAL KIDNAPPINGS OFF STREETS
IN SETAGAYA

46
00:04:03,142 --> 00:04:04,677
NAME: SOTA YUKIMURA

47
00:04:04,744 --> 00:04:07,247
The fact that I was present
at two murder scenes…

48
00:04:08,348 --> 00:04:09,282
I think it was also due

49
00:04:09,949 --> 00:04:14,887
to someone's intention,
someone pulling the strings.

50
00:04:38,745 --> 00:04:40,346
Wow, this is amazing.

51
00:04:40,413 --> 00:04:41,781
It doesn't use PET at all.

52
00:04:41,848 --> 00:04:44,717
That's right. It's composed of Melittin,

53
00:04:44,784 --> 00:04:46,753
which gives it its lightness.

54
00:04:46,819 --> 00:04:50,623
It's pretty boundary-pushing,
even in terms of price range.

55
00:04:51,457 --> 00:04:53,293
This will definitely sell.

56
00:04:56,095 --> 00:04:57,196
Goodbye.

57
00:04:57,263 --> 00:04:58,998
-See you.
-Goodbye.

58
00:05:01,801 --> 00:05:03,069
Bye.

59
00:05:03,136 --> 00:05:05,038
-Goodbye.
-Bye.

60
00:05:15,782 --> 00:05:17,817
He lives alone, doesn't he?

61
00:05:18,685 --> 00:05:21,154
So why is he buying so much?

62
00:05:23,089 --> 00:05:24,090
So?

63
00:05:24,157 --> 00:05:26,993
What on earth are you doing?

64
00:05:28,361 --> 00:05:29,562
Hey, hey, hey.

65
00:05:31,130 --> 00:05:33,333
Should we keep an eye on that guy?

66
00:05:34,467 --> 00:05:35,535
Yes…

67
00:05:36,836 --> 00:05:39,105
He was investigating me
without my knowledge.

68
00:05:40,473 --> 00:05:43,142
He might be a very dangerous person.

69
00:05:43,209 --> 00:05:46,145
It looks like he even checked
my social media.

70
00:05:46,212 --> 00:05:47,747
He was creeping around?

71
00:05:48,348 --> 00:05:50,350
So what does that mean, he's a stalker?

72
00:05:51,317 --> 00:05:53,319
He's even been questioned by the police.

73
00:05:53,953 --> 00:05:55,621
We can't let our guard down.

74
00:05:55,688 --> 00:05:56,956
-I'll throw these in.
-Wow.

75
00:05:57,023 --> 00:06:01,294
I'm a manager, so I need to know
for the safety of everyone at work

76
00:06:01,361 --> 00:06:03,496
-Ah, he moved.
-Let's follow him.

77
00:06:09,669 --> 00:06:13,439
At this rate,
you look more like a stalker.

78
00:06:14,273 --> 00:06:15,408
Me?

79
00:06:16,409 --> 00:06:18,311
It can't be helped.

80
00:06:18,378 --> 00:06:21,581
You want to know everything
about the person you like, right?

81
00:06:22,782 --> 00:06:25,585
Ah, well, I have experience with that too.

82
00:06:25,651 --> 00:06:28,788
-Was it back in middle school…
-I am a manager!

83
00:06:37,096 --> 00:06:39,031
What is he looking at?

84
00:06:39,098 --> 00:06:40,099
LOOKING FOR DOG

85
00:06:40,166 --> 00:06:41,100
"He's friendly…"

86
00:06:41,167 --> 00:06:42,101
GRILLED MEAT

87
00:06:42,168 --> 00:06:43,102
MUSHROOMS

88
00:06:45,204 --> 00:06:47,607
-Oh, oh, oh!
-Oh!

89
00:06:47,673 --> 00:06:48,941
Oh, no!

90
00:06:49,542 --> 00:06:50,576
Are you okay?

91
00:06:50,643 --> 00:06:52,345
I'm sorry, I'm sorry…

92
00:06:52,412 --> 00:06:54,180
Thank you.

93
00:06:54,247 --> 00:06:55,848
-You're a lifesaver.
-Are you okay now?

94
00:06:55,915 --> 00:06:57,884
-Thank you!
-No, it was no problem.

95
00:06:57,950 --> 00:06:59,419
-Over this way.
-I see.

96
00:06:59,485 --> 00:07:02,488
-How about some tea?
-Kind to the elderly.

97
00:07:02,555 --> 00:07:03,389
-Well…
-That's okay.

98
00:07:03,456 --> 00:07:04,590
High points, huh?

99
00:07:04,657 --> 00:07:06,392
That's right.

100
00:07:06,459 --> 00:07:08,995
Kind people really are the best.

101
00:07:10,463 --> 00:07:11,964
Hmm, I see…

102
00:07:20,606 --> 00:07:21,507
Let's go.

103
00:07:28,481 --> 00:07:31,350
Why has he been here so long?

104
00:07:32,151 --> 00:07:34,320
It's been quite a while.

105
00:07:34,387 --> 00:07:39,025
He's not suspicious or anything
like that, but I'm worried now.

106
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:43,629
Now that I've stopped
investigating Mariko,

107
00:07:44,430 --> 00:07:48,401
I have insane amounts of time on my hands.

108
00:07:49,569 --> 00:07:52,839
Assuming the average
male lifespan is 80 years,

109
00:07:52,905 --> 00:07:55,141
I've got 49 more years to go.

110
00:07:55,208 --> 00:07:58,945
Working eight hours a day,
sleeping seven hours.

111
00:07:59,879 --> 00:08:02,048
Remaining nine hours of free time,

112
00:08:02,114 --> 00:08:04,784
multiplied by 49 years.

113
00:08:05,485 --> 00:08:07,653
What should I spend them doing?

114
00:08:08,354 --> 00:08:12,024
So that I don't end up looking into
Mariko, I should start a new hobby.

115
00:08:12,925 --> 00:08:14,794
Movies… I'll watch movies or something!

116
00:08:16,562 --> 00:08:17,730
Marvel…

117
00:08:18,831 --> 00:08:20,066
Mariko…

118
00:08:20,566 --> 00:08:21,534
What?

119
00:08:22,335 --> 00:08:24,203
Should I start taking lessons?

120
00:08:24,270 --> 00:08:25,404
Coffee classes?

121
00:08:25,471 --> 00:08:26,572
What, what?

122
00:08:27,473 --> 00:08:30,343
Coffee… Cafe latte…

123
00:08:30,977 --> 00:08:32,245
Mariko…

124
00:08:32,311 --> 00:08:34,146
What?

125
00:08:34,213 --> 00:08:37,583
I wonder if I can donate my time
to people in this world

126
00:08:38,184 --> 00:08:41,120
who are struggling
with not having enough time.

127
00:08:45,691 --> 00:08:48,094
I'm hungry.

128
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:50,830
I bet you are. Shall we go home?

129
00:08:53,466 --> 00:08:55,368
-Sota!
-It's Tomoya!

130
00:08:55,434 --> 00:08:57,737
-Tomoya!
-Huh?

131
00:08:57,803 --> 00:09:00,606
-Do you know her?
-What's everyone doing here?

132
00:09:02,275 --> 00:09:03,843
Is this Izumi's daughter?

133
00:09:04,443 --> 00:09:06,412
Yes, this is Sara.

134
00:09:06,479 --> 00:09:07,914
Hello.

135
00:09:07,980 --> 00:09:09,215
She's Sara.

136
00:09:09,949 --> 00:09:11,217
Hello.

137
00:09:12,985 --> 00:09:15,955
So, what are you all doing
in a place like this?

138
00:09:16,022 --> 00:09:17,890
We just were around.

139
00:09:19,091 --> 00:09:19,926
A coincidence.

140
00:09:19,992 --> 00:09:22,762
We just happened to be passing by.

141
00:09:22,828 --> 00:09:24,597
-Oh, really?
-Really, we just happened to be here.

142
00:09:29,302 --> 00:09:30,436
Well then,

143
00:09:31,003 --> 00:09:32,972
-why don't we all eat together?
-Right?

144
00:09:33,039 --> 00:09:33,873
Yes, let's go!

145
00:09:33,940 --> 00:09:36,075
-Yes, let's do that!
-Yes.

146
00:09:37,043 --> 00:09:38,277
Ah, I'm sorry,

147
00:09:38,344 --> 00:09:39,645
-I'm leaving.
-Huh?

148
00:09:40,880 --> 00:09:42,815
Hey. Sota.

149
00:09:45,084 --> 00:09:47,019
Why don't we go home too?

150
00:09:47,086 --> 00:09:48,254
What?

151
00:09:51,023 --> 00:09:51,958
Hey!

152
00:09:56,462 --> 00:09:58,864
TAISUKE SAKURA

153
00:10:04,937 --> 00:10:05,905
MARIKO NOSE

154
00:10:09,609 --> 00:10:11,777
GINJIRO NOSE

155
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:18,551
This is Sakura from the Tokyo
Metropolitan Police Department.

156
00:10:22,021 --> 00:10:23,589
That was a great idea I had.

157
00:10:23,656 --> 00:10:25,291
What did you do that for?

158
00:10:25,358 --> 00:10:27,593
-Sorry.
-That seemed like something

159
00:10:27,660 --> 00:10:30,329
Mariko would have been into too,
but then it was ruined.

160
00:10:30,396 --> 00:10:31,530
Do you want the dumplings boiled or fried?

161
00:10:33,032 --> 00:10:34,500
Uh, fried.

162
00:11:17,677 --> 00:11:18,811
What are you doing?

163
00:11:19,412 --> 00:11:21,380
No, nothing.

164
00:11:26,585 --> 00:11:27,520
Did you read them?

165
00:11:28,854 --> 00:11:31,524
Not yet. I just wondered what they were,

166
00:11:32,625 --> 00:11:33,526
so I held it for a second.

167
00:11:36,429 --> 00:11:37,997
Seriously, I swear to God.

168
00:11:46,272 --> 00:11:49,041
Come to think of it, I meant to tell you
the other day, but couldn't.

169
00:11:49,108 --> 00:11:50,843
I got a huge piece of info.

170
00:11:50,910 --> 00:11:52,278
-A huge piece of info?
-Yeah.

171
00:11:52,344 --> 00:11:54,647
Um, at that Sayuri person's funeral,

172
00:11:54,714 --> 00:11:58,150
I overheard Mariko
and her younger brother talking.

173
00:11:58,718 --> 00:12:00,386
Sayuri said to the president,

174
00:12:00,953 --> 00:12:07,927
"You haven't forgotten that you and I
share the same secret, have you?"

175
00:12:08,961 --> 00:12:10,262
The same secret?

176
00:12:11,230 --> 00:12:12,665
I just gave you crazy info, right?

177
00:12:12,732 --> 00:12:14,266
You could investigate it--

178
00:12:14,333 --> 00:12:16,435
-No, it's fine.
-Huh?

179
00:12:16,969 --> 00:12:19,705
That's not something for me to do.

180
00:12:21,207 --> 00:12:22,541
The police…

181
00:12:23,676 --> 00:12:25,344
That detective is on it.

182
00:12:26,946 --> 00:12:28,280
I shouldn't do it.

183
00:12:29,648 --> 00:12:31,083
What?

184
00:12:31,150 --> 00:12:32,051
I mean,

185
00:12:32,585 --> 00:12:36,922
two people in her circle have been killed,
and right now, Mariko might be in danger.

186
00:12:36,989 --> 00:12:38,290
I can't.

187
00:12:39,658 --> 00:12:41,894
It's not something I should do.

188
00:12:50,703 --> 00:12:53,639
I shouldn't have spoken to her that day.

189
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:56,475
You can put hers together with mine.

190
00:12:59,645 --> 00:13:03,048
I was a person who shouldn't
have appeared before Mariko.

191
00:13:04,550 --> 00:13:08,187
No, I guess meeting 25 years ago

192
00:13:08,254 --> 00:13:11,423
and falling in love with her was wrong.

193
00:13:11,490 --> 00:13:13,692
That's not it.

194
00:13:14,293 --> 00:13:15,895
That's not where your mistake is.

195
00:13:17,830 --> 00:13:20,065
Actually, you've been wrong
the whole time.

196
00:13:20,132 --> 00:13:22,001
You've done nothing but wrong things.

197
00:13:23,402 --> 00:13:25,671
So why are you trying to act proper
all of a sudden?

198
00:13:32,878 --> 00:13:35,981
You know, I really hate that part of you.

199
00:13:36,682 --> 00:13:38,651
Why are you backing off?

200
00:13:40,286 --> 00:13:42,988
You've loved her
for 25 years, right? Twenty-five years!

201
00:13:43,656 --> 00:13:45,858
Even if you back off,
it's not like your feelings will subside.

202
00:13:46,559 --> 00:13:47,993
If you take Mariko away from your life,

203
00:13:48,060 --> 00:13:51,530
-what's left for you?
-I don't want to scare Mariko anymore!

204
00:13:52,431 --> 00:13:53,866
It was all wrong.

205
00:13:54,867 --> 00:13:56,302
All of it.

206
00:13:56,368 --> 00:14:00,773
I'm not allowed to move forward,
nor to go back.

207
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:05,144
Then, at that company, in that department,

208
00:14:05,744 --> 00:14:08,714
just treat her normally,
like a normal person would.

209
00:14:09,748 --> 00:14:10,816
Stop sneaking around in secret

210
00:14:10,883 --> 00:14:13,552
-and just interact with her normally.
-That's impossible for me.

211
00:14:13,619 --> 00:14:15,287
Whenever Mariko
is in trouble or suffering,

212
00:14:15,354 --> 00:14:16,689
I end up wanting to do something.

213
00:14:17,256 --> 00:14:18,190
It's just like a diet.

214
00:14:18,257 --> 00:14:20,593
When you're told you can eat just a bit,
holding back is extremely painful,

215
00:14:20,659 --> 00:14:23,696
but if it's completely off-limits,
looking or getting close is off-limits,

216
00:14:23,762 --> 00:14:26,298
then I can think of it as something
that doesn't exist in this world.

217
00:14:27,399 --> 00:14:29,134
That's why it's better
not to get involved anymore.

218
00:14:29,702 --> 00:14:30,936
What the hell is that?

219
00:14:31,003 --> 00:14:33,739
What is with you? I don't give a damn.
I've never been on a diet!

220
00:14:36,942 --> 00:14:41,213
You know, I'm sick and tired of listening
to your endless rambling excuses.

221
00:14:43,883 --> 00:14:46,418
You've never faced Mariko
in a proper way to begin with.

222
00:14:47,052 --> 00:14:48,654
Why are you trying to act proper now?

223
00:14:49,722 --> 00:14:52,358
-But--
-You're the one who has protected her.

224
00:14:53,292 --> 00:14:56,862
Listen, what will you do
if she actually is in danger right now?

225
00:14:57,696 --> 00:15:00,232
Are you going to leave it to some
other guy who randomly popped up?

226
00:15:00,299 --> 00:15:02,401
You're gonna ignore it?
You're out of your mind!

227
00:15:04,703 --> 00:15:06,739
You're saying weird things too, Tomoya.

228
00:15:07,273 --> 00:15:08,707
Telling me to date her
normally one moment,

229
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:11,877
-then to not to pretend to be normal--
-I don't care

230
00:15:11,944 --> 00:15:14,680
whether you're a stalker
or whether Mariko hates you!

231
00:15:17,549 --> 00:15:20,119
Even so, protecting Mariko
is your job, isn't it?

232
00:15:25,858 --> 00:15:27,159
I'm going home.

233
00:15:59,625 --> 00:16:00,793
I'm home.

234
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:02,828
Welcome back.

235
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:09,468
Where's Keito?

236
00:16:09,535 --> 00:16:11,637
He said he was going to a friend's place.

237
00:16:12,938 --> 00:16:14,039
I see…

238
00:16:14,106 --> 00:16:17,009
I wonder if that boy's okay.

239
00:16:18,043 --> 00:16:20,612
I guess he wouldn't be…

240
00:16:21,747 --> 00:16:23,615
Oh, Mariko, you're home?

241
00:16:24,550 --> 00:16:26,018
I have something to talk about.

242
00:16:28,153 --> 00:16:29,121
Mariko.

243
00:16:29,188 --> 00:16:32,691
Sakura, why are you at our home?

244
00:16:36,695 --> 00:16:38,263
-Thank you.
-Sure.

245
00:16:40,065 --> 00:16:41,300
I see.

246
00:16:41,367 --> 00:16:44,470
You helped my mother at first, and then…

247
00:16:45,237 --> 00:16:46,338
That's right.

248
00:16:46,872 --> 00:16:49,375
Who would have thought
a kind-hearted passerby

249
00:16:49,441 --> 00:16:54,380
would turn out to be a detective.

250
00:16:54,446 --> 00:16:59,618
If Sakura is by Mariko's side,
I can rest easy as well.

251
00:16:59,685 --> 00:17:02,821
Please take good care
of her going forward.

252
00:17:02,888 --> 00:17:03,722
Dad!

253
00:17:03,789 --> 00:17:05,624
Please raise your head.

254
00:17:09,261 --> 00:17:11,330
REST IN PEACE

255
00:17:25,644 --> 00:17:27,846
Where were you going, Mariko?

256
00:17:28,747 --> 00:17:30,215
I called, but…

257
00:17:31,116 --> 00:17:33,852
I'm sorry, I was dealing with something.

258
00:17:35,120 --> 00:17:38,891
We should be together as much
as possible until the case is solved.

259
00:17:42,127 --> 00:17:43,896
I know it's annoying.

260
00:17:44,863 --> 00:17:49,401
And I know you clearly told me you didn't
want me walking you home the other day…

261
00:17:51,303 --> 00:17:52,871
But I'm worried.

262
00:17:53,505 --> 00:17:54,807
This time for sure…

263
00:17:57,409 --> 00:17:59,078
I will protect you.

264
00:18:03,949 --> 00:18:05,150
This time?

265
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:09,455
That reminds me.

266
00:18:10,456 --> 00:18:15,027
Influenced by you,
I've started painting again recently.

267
00:18:15,594 --> 00:18:16,795
Influenced by me?

268
00:18:16,862 --> 00:18:18,130
I'll show you sometime.

269
00:18:21,433 --> 00:18:23,168
SHIRAKI

270
00:18:23,869 --> 00:18:25,003
Excuse me for a moment.

271
00:18:26,538 --> 00:18:28,440
Yes, hello?

272
00:18:30,275 --> 00:18:31,110
‎Yes.

273
00:18:32,377 --> 00:18:33,212
‎Yes…

274
00:18:35,681 --> 00:18:36,515
What?

275
00:18:37,716 --> 00:18:38,550
Understood.

276
00:18:40,686 --> 00:18:43,322
Asai has been taken
into protective custody.

277
00:18:44,490 --> 00:18:45,557
What?

278
00:18:53,065 --> 00:18:56,735
If he doesn't regain consciousness soon,
he'll have to be hospitalized even longer.

279
00:18:56,802 --> 00:18:58,337
He will live.

280
00:18:58,871 --> 00:19:00,038
Thank you very much.

281
00:19:00,105 --> 00:19:02,374
-Please take care of him.
-Please.

282
00:19:02,441 --> 00:19:03,475
-Doctor.
-Yes?

283
00:19:03,542 --> 00:19:05,377
-May I have a moment?
-Yes.

284
00:19:10,582 --> 00:19:13,452
To think this could happen to Asai.

285
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:16,288
Who would do something like this?

286
00:19:19,591 --> 00:19:22,561
Was it the same one
who killed Tateiwa and Sayuri?

287
00:19:23,996 --> 00:19:26,899
That I do not know. However…

288
00:19:31,136 --> 00:19:32,204
No.

289
00:19:32,271 --> 00:19:33,272
What?

290
00:19:34,740 --> 00:19:37,009
You have a lot of secrets.

291
00:19:37,943 --> 00:19:42,080
I came home today because
I wanted to ask you something.

292
00:19:43,515 --> 00:19:45,284
Keito said he heard it.

293
00:19:47,219 --> 00:19:50,022
What is the secret you and Sayuri share?

294
00:19:51,590 --> 00:19:53,825
You haven't forgotten, have you?

295
00:19:54,393 --> 00:19:58,263
That you and I share the same secret.

296
00:19:59,765 --> 00:20:02,100
Isn't it something related
to what's happened?

297
00:20:02,634 --> 00:20:04,336
Hey, Dad!

298
00:20:04,403 --> 00:20:06,205
Stop keeping secrets from me!

299
00:20:26,758 --> 00:20:28,093
Which one is it?

300
00:20:31,129 --> 00:20:35,334
Regarding Kagura, we were able to secure
distribution in 100 stores for now.

301
00:20:36,768 --> 00:20:41,206
Also for EC, next Monday
is when they'll buy,

302
00:20:41,273 --> 00:20:45,244
so we at least hope to have
a selection ready for them.

303
00:20:45,310 --> 00:20:47,379
What do we think about that?

304
00:20:50,349 --> 00:20:51,717
Mariko?

305
00:20:55,654 --> 00:20:57,022
Ah, um…

306
00:20:57,089 --> 00:20:57,956
I'm sorry.

307
00:20:58,490 --> 00:20:59,825
One more time, please.

308
00:20:59,891 --> 00:21:00,726
Okay.

309
00:21:01,526 --> 00:21:02,728
Let's see. Previous page…

310
00:21:03,228 --> 00:21:07,466
Regarding Kagura, we were able to secure
distribution in 100 stores for now.

311
00:21:29,087 --> 00:21:30,355
Goodbye, everyone.

312
00:21:30,422 --> 00:21:32,491
-Goodbye.
-See you.

313
00:21:49,574 --> 00:21:50,642
Mariko.

314
00:21:52,177 --> 00:21:54,246
You forgot this on your desk.

315
00:21:54,313 --> 00:21:56,581
Huh? Oh, thank you.

316
00:21:58,016 --> 00:21:58,950
Are you okay?

317
00:21:59,685 --> 00:22:01,053
Did something happen?

318
00:22:03,121 --> 00:22:03,989
I'm sorry.

319
00:22:04,723 --> 00:22:06,091
It's none of my business.

320
00:22:29,548 --> 00:22:30,682
Hello.

321
00:22:32,084 --> 00:22:34,353
-Chairwoman, what brings you here?
-Are you alone?

322
00:22:35,120 --> 00:22:36,421
If you want Mariko, she already…

323
00:22:36,488 --> 00:22:38,390
I came to see you.

324
00:22:43,028 --> 00:22:47,099
The incident with Tateiwa and Sayuri.

325
00:22:47,966 --> 00:22:50,435
I heard you were questioned by the police?

326
00:22:52,237 --> 00:22:53,238
Yes.

327
00:22:54,106 --> 00:22:55,207
Did you do it?

328
00:22:57,376 --> 00:22:59,678
Of course not. I know that.

329
00:23:03,782 --> 00:23:07,352
Is our family cursed or something?

330
00:23:07,953 --> 00:23:09,588
Two daughters-in-law.

331
00:23:10,255 --> 00:23:14,359
Even a daughter-in-law I hated
so much, for her to die like that…

332
00:23:15,227 --> 00:23:17,462
Why did you hate her so much?

333
00:23:19,598 --> 00:23:21,199
Sorry, I shouldn't pry.

334
00:23:23,301 --> 00:23:26,671
Kyoko, Mariko's biological mother,

335
00:23:27,305 --> 00:23:28,940
was suspected of having an affair.

336
00:23:29,574 --> 00:23:30,409
What?

337
00:23:30,475 --> 00:23:35,213
I don't know who it was with,
but Ginjiro seemed to suspect

338
00:23:35,280 --> 00:23:37,682
it was with a younger man.

339
00:23:38,350 --> 00:23:40,719
I think that was a lie.

340
00:23:41,586 --> 00:23:42,854
And yet,

341
00:23:43,522 --> 00:23:47,626
Sayuri said that to young Mariko,

342
00:23:48,193 --> 00:23:52,731
of all places, at Kyoko's funeral.

343
00:23:53,432 --> 00:23:58,069
Your mother fell in love with another man.

344
00:23:59,337 --> 00:24:00,505
Poor thing.

345
00:24:03,508 --> 00:24:05,243
Thinking about what feelings

346
00:24:06,611 --> 00:24:09,614
Mariko has lived with since then.

347
00:24:09,681 --> 00:24:11,850
Mariko's mother wasn't
that kind of person.

348
00:24:12,417 --> 00:24:13,685
It's definitely not true.

349
00:24:15,387 --> 00:24:16,721
I know Mariko's mother.

350
00:24:18,857 --> 00:24:19,758
Um…

351
00:24:20,459 --> 00:24:22,260
I've been…

352
00:24:23,895 --> 00:24:25,564
I've been watching Mariko this whole time.

353
00:24:26,264 --> 00:24:27,199
What?

354
00:24:28,266 --> 00:24:29,868
I wanted to be with Mariko,

355
00:24:29,935 --> 00:24:32,270
so I went to the same middle school,
high school, university,

356
00:24:33,138 --> 00:24:36,641
and even followed her to the same company.

357
00:24:38,009 --> 00:24:40,445
But I could never talk to her even once.

358
00:24:42,013 --> 00:24:43,615
All I could do was just watch her.

359
00:24:46,685 --> 00:24:47,919
I've loved…

360
00:24:50,055 --> 00:24:52,023
Mariko for so long.

361
00:24:54,359 --> 00:24:57,395
Confessing to me isn't going to do much.

362
00:24:59,164 --> 00:25:02,634
Do you love Mariko that much?

363
00:25:04,202 --> 00:25:05,937
Yes, I'm sorry.

364
00:25:07,038 --> 00:25:10,275
Hearing someone say
they love my grandchild

365
00:25:10,342 --> 00:25:12,477
doesn't feel bad.

366
00:25:13,879 --> 00:25:15,480
She's a good girl, isn't she?

367
00:25:16,815 --> 00:25:20,719
But if you love her so much,
why didn't you ever speak to her?

368
00:25:22,320 --> 00:25:26,491
There must have been plenty of times
you could have said something.

369
00:25:26,558 --> 00:25:27,726
Well, that's…

370
00:25:28,860 --> 00:25:32,130
Mariko is someone I admire, so…

371
00:25:33,398 --> 00:25:34,966
Just watching her was enough.

372
00:25:35,500 --> 00:25:38,803
If Mariko was happy,
that alone made me happy.

373
00:25:40,772 --> 00:25:42,507
You're not being honest.

374
00:25:45,210 --> 00:25:51,416
When things don't go well,
the cause is always within yourself.

375
00:25:52,484 --> 00:25:56,955
You shouldn't look for answers
inside the other person.

376
00:26:12,070 --> 00:26:13,505
Sorry about that.

377
00:26:15,774 --> 00:26:17,142
Wait here a second.

378
00:26:18,443 --> 00:26:19,678
Ah, no, no, it's fine.

379
00:26:19,744 --> 00:26:21,179
It'd be terrible if you got hurt.

380
00:26:27,619 --> 00:26:30,488
It's rare to see you irritated.

381
00:26:32,557 --> 00:26:33,658
Sorry.

382
00:26:34,826 --> 00:26:36,294
Days like that happen.

383
00:26:36,361 --> 00:26:37,596
We're human, after all.

384
00:26:44,769 --> 00:26:45,604
After all?

385
00:26:47,238 --> 00:26:49,941
I get irritated all the time.

386
00:26:50,008 --> 00:26:51,509
Like when everything doesn't fit

387
00:26:51,576 --> 00:26:54,079
into the reusable bag
I brought to the supermarket

388
00:26:54,145 --> 00:26:56,581
and I have to buy a plastic bag.

389
00:26:57,649 --> 00:27:01,753
Or thinking, "Ah, I didn't even need
to buy this mirin today, damn it."

390
00:27:02,787 --> 00:27:07,025
Or when an elevator door is closing,

391
00:27:07,092 --> 00:27:12,530
and someone rushes up, hits the button
to force it open, and gets in.

392
00:27:14,466 --> 00:27:16,501
I guess that's not being irritated.

393
00:27:16,568 --> 00:27:18,837
That's just me having a bad personality.

394
00:27:22,440 --> 00:27:23,608
Thank you.

395
00:27:26,511 --> 00:27:28,613
If you want to talk about it, I'll listen.

396
00:27:33,818 --> 00:27:34,819
Mama!

397
00:27:38,156 --> 00:27:39,024
Coming.

398
00:27:40,525 --> 00:27:42,027
What were you talking about?

399
00:27:42,093 --> 00:27:44,963
Huh? It's a secret. Let's go home.

400
00:28:05,250 --> 00:28:06,951
SATORU HATANO

401
00:28:07,018 --> 00:28:08,620
HE MAY BE DANGEROUS

402
00:28:08,687 --> 00:28:12,757
HE'S THE ONE WHO TRIED TO KIDNAP MARIKO

403
00:29:43,515 --> 00:29:44,949
MARIKO NOSE

404
00:29:52,991 --> 00:29:55,860
COME QUICK
I'LL KILL HER IF YOU TELL ANYONE

405
00:30:23,321 --> 00:30:24,455
Mariko!

406
00:31:16,407 --> 00:31:18,176
GOTO ASAI - NOSE COSMETICS

407
00:31:23,982 --> 00:31:25,650
MARIKO NOSE - NOSE COSMETICS

408
00:31:35,627 --> 00:31:37,896
-The number you have dialed…
-Shit…

409
00:31:55,880 --> 00:31:57,615
It's okay.

410
00:31:59,350 --> 00:32:02,186
I won't kill you, princess.

411
00:32:03,187 --> 00:32:06,858
Well, if I end up killing you
along the way, my bad.

412
00:32:11,896 --> 00:32:14,265
You've gotten big.

413
00:32:16,100 --> 00:32:17,502
What on earth

414
00:32:18,569 --> 00:32:20,038
are you planning to do?

415
00:32:24,976 --> 00:32:26,377
Mariko!

416
00:32:26,444 --> 00:32:29,047
Yukimura! Why?

417
00:32:29,113 --> 00:32:31,049
You finally showed up.

418
00:32:31,115 --> 00:32:32,951
Get away from Mariko.

419
00:32:34,152 --> 00:32:36,721
-Get away!
-It's fine.

420
00:32:36,788 --> 00:32:38,656
Calm down.

421
00:32:38,723 --> 00:32:41,159
The one getting killed is you, after all.

422
00:32:43,795 --> 00:32:46,331
I've wanted to meet you
for a long time, boy.

423
00:32:47,832 --> 00:32:51,736
Thanks to that courageous action of yours,

424
00:32:51,803 --> 00:32:54,572
I had to spend 25 years in prison.

425
00:32:55,840 --> 00:32:57,976
Coming out after all this time,

426
00:32:58,042 --> 00:33:02,613
the world has changed
so much that it blew my mind.

427
00:33:02,680 --> 00:33:05,183
Even in Shibuya,
there aren't any kogals left at all.

428
00:33:05,249 --> 00:33:07,752
And it's Toyosu Market now, not Tsukiji.

429
00:33:08,586 --> 00:33:11,656
The biggest thing is security cameras.

430
00:33:12,190 --> 00:33:13,891
They're everywhere.

431
00:33:14,792 --> 00:33:18,062
You can't just easily kidnap
someone like in the old days.

432
00:33:18,730 --> 00:33:21,466
It's a tough world to live in. Right?

433
00:33:23,001 --> 00:33:26,904
But some things don't change.

434
00:33:28,840 --> 00:33:31,142
I was moved, boy.

435
00:33:32,276 --> 00:33:34,679
I thought you were just
some kid passing by,

436
00:33:34,746 --> 00:33:38,683
but here you are even now,
coming to save the princess in a pinch.

437
00:33:39,917 --> 00:33:42,286
You're a fine hero.

438
00:33:44,789 --> 00:33:47,592
Makes it worth doing for me too.

439
00:33:48,426 --> 00:33:51,129
I understand very well
that your target is me.

440
00:33:51,662 --> 00:33:54,365
So please let Mariko go right now.

441
00:33:54,432 --> 00:33:56,601
After that, you can kill me.

442
00:33:56,667 --> 00:33:58,202
What are you saying?

443
00:33:59,637 --> 00:34:01,005
You're amazing.

444
00:34:02,173 --> 00:34:04,742
You're a far braver boy than I imagined.

445
00:34:04,809 --> 00:34:07,612
Stop it! Yukimura, run away, quick!

446
00:34:07,678 --> 00:34:09,881
Please let Mariko go.

447
00:34:10,615 --> 00:34:12,717
How cool.

448
00:34:13,217 --> 00:34:18,089
But wouldn't showing her
a man dying for her sake

449
00:34:18,156 --> 00:34:19,857
be even cooler?

450
00:34:19,924 --> 00:34:22,560
Right?

451
00:34:22,627 --> 00:34:23,494
Don't move.

452
00:34:48,052 --> 00:34:48,986
Mariko.

453
00:34:49,053 --> 00:34:50,488
Are you okay?

454
00:34:56,494 --> 00:34:57,562
Yukimura, behind you!

455
00:35:04,969 --> 00:35:08,906
You've got a disastrous life too.

456
00:35:10,041 --> 00:35:11,109
If you hadn't

457
00:35:11,909 --> 00:35:14,512
witnessed this princess'
kidnapping back then,

458
00:35:14,579 --> 00:35:17,115
you wouldn't have to die here.

459
00:35:18,282 --> 00:35:20,485
My life…

460
00:35:21,085 --> 00:35:23,121
isn't a disaster!

461
00:35:29,527 --> 00:35:30,261
Yukimura!

462
00:35:37,768 --> 00:35:39,237
Yukimura!

463
00:36:33,991 --> 00:36:36,060
That hurt!

464
00:36:36,694 --> 00:36:37,528
Mariko…

465
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:44,035
Mariko!

466
00:36:45,403 --> 00:36:48,639
Hey, stay back.

467
00:36:48,706 --> 00:36:50,107
Get away from Mariko!

468
00:36:52,643 --> 00:36:54,111
Police!

469
00:36:55,279 --> 00:36:57,949
Hatano, release the hostage.

470
00:37:00,418 --> 00:37:01,519
Release her, now!

471
00:37:03,321 --> 00:37:05,389
-Shut up!
-Don't move!

472
00:37:06,724 --> 00:37:07,858
Get back.

473
00:37:08,893 --> 00:37:10,261
Go away!

474
00:37:10,328 --> 00:37:12,396
Go away!

475
00:37:12,463 --> 00:37:14,198
-Let her go!
-Stay back!

476
00:37:17,301 --> 00:37:18,903
Stop! Hatano, stop!

477
00:37:18,970 --> 00:37:20,871
Mariko, are you okay?

478
00:37:21,372 --> 00:37:23,107
-Are you hurt?
-I'm fine.

479
00:37:23,174 --> 00:37:24,809
You're not okay, though, evidently.

480
00:37:26,043 --> 00:37:29,380
One man fled the scene, two victims.

481
00:37:29,447 --> 00:37:30,615
They're conscious.

482
00:37:30,681 --> 00:37:32,550
Requesting an ambulance.

483
00:37:35,019 --> 00:37:36,821
Mariko, are you hurt?

484
00:37:36,887 --> 00:37:38,823
I'm fine.

485
00:37:38,889 --> 00:37:40,057
Thank goodness…

486
00:37:41,859 --> 00:37:42,760
Sorry…

487
00:37:42,827 --> 00:37:43,961
Yukimura…

488
00:37:52,203 --> 00:37:53,471
I'll tie it.

489
00:37:57,108 --> 00:37:59,076
An ambulance will be here shortly.

490
00:37:59,143 --> 00:38:00,177
Okay.

491
00:38:09,954 --> 00:38:13,457
‎POLICE

492
00:38:13,524 --> 00:38:16,794
‎STOPPING CRIME

493
00:38:38,182 --> 00:38:39,950
Why would you do something that dangerous?

494
00:38:42,186 --> 00:38:46,190
You could've contacted the police
or anything else, right?

495
00:38:47,425 --> 00:38:48,459
I'm sorry.

496
00:38:57,335 --> 00:38:58,269
You…

497
00:39:01,105 --> 00:39:04,508
were the boy
who saved me back then, right?

498
00:39:09,080 --> 00:39:09,914
Yes.

499
00:39:12,283 --> 00:39:13,184
Why?

500
00:39:17,788 --> 00:39:18,989
Why didn't you say anything?

501
00:39:24,295 --> 00:39:26,130
You could have told me at any point.

502
00:39:27,131 --> 00:39:31,302
Twenty-five years ago, or even since
we've known each other.

503
00:39:42,012 --> 00:39:44,382
I had no courage.

504
00:39:45,883 --> 00:39:50,421
Ever since I was a child, I was the kind
of kid who couldn't even talk back

505
00:39:50,488 --> 00:39:51,922
when classmates made fun of me.

506
00:39:53,924 --> 00:39:57,027
Even if I talked to you,
I didn't think you'd like me.

507
00:39:57,895 --> 00:39:59,029
In fact…

508
00:40:01,132 --> 00:40:02,767
I thought you might hate me.

509
00:40:05,736 --> 00:40:07,238
But I…

510
00:40:10,207 --> 00:40:12,243
I'd always wanted to talk to you,

511
00:40:14,111 --> 00:40:15,579
but I didn't have the courage.

512
00:40:18,849 --> 00:40:20,551
Even though you can do
something like this?

513
00:40:23,821 --> 00:40:26,590
I can't do anything for myself.

514
00:40:29,093 --> 00:40:30,895
But if it's for your sake, Mariko…

515
00:40:34,365 --> 00:40:36,867
That's what scares you, isn't it?

516
00:40:36,934 --> 00:40:38,035
I'm sorry.

517
00:40:38,903 --> 00:40:39,770
No,

518
00:40:40,571 --> 00:40:42,072
it's not that you scare me.

519
00:40:45,109 --> 00:40:48,746
It's that I don't know
who the real you is anymore.

520
00:40:50,047 --> 00:40:51,415
That's why I got scared.

521
00:40:53,217 --> 00:40:56,520
I mean, like with Marvel
and cafes and stuff,

522
00:40:57,087 --> 00:40:59,623
you only liked them
because I liked them, right?

523
00:41:00,224 --> 00:41:02,259
That's not the real you.

524
00:41:25,049 --> 00:41:25,950
This…

525
00:41:27,885 --> 00:41:28,953
is me.

526
00:41:32,223 --> 00:41:36,060
I came to like what you liked,

527
00:41:38,362 --> 00:41:40,030
look at the scenery you looked at.

528
00:41:41,565 --> 00:41:43,234
That's how I've lived.

529
00:41:47,972 --> 00:41:51,876
If I lose you, Mariko,
I will have nothing left in my life.

530
00:41:53,777 --> 00:41:56,814
Because ever since you appeared
in my life, right up to today…

531
00:42:01,218 --> 00:42:03,888
I've always been happy.

532
00:42:08,325 --> 00:42:11,562
I'm living my own life…

533
00:42:16,400 --> 00:42:18,269
but you've always been in it, Mariko.

534
00:42:23,807 --> 00:42:24,909
I'm sorry.

535
00:42:27,044 --> 00:42:28,946
For watching over you for 25 years…

536
00:42:31,315 --> 00:42:33,183
without you asking me to.

537
00:42:38,589 --> 00:42:39,990
I'm sorry.

538
00:42:47,698 --> 00:42:49,433
You really are scary.

539
00:43:24,501 --> 00:43:28,572
-Ready? Let's go.
-Yes.

540
00:43:29,373 --> 00:43:32,876
Whoa, Mom's going to get mad at us.

541
00:43:32,943 --> 00:43:34,411
Because you're terrible at this.

542
00:43:35,245 --> 00:43:37,247
That's because you didn't
catch it properly, Tomoya!

543
00:43:37,314 --> 00:43:39,984
-You suck!
-Shut up!

544
00:44:16,687 --> 00:44:18,255
Wait, wait!

545
00:44:19,623 --> 00:44:22,826
Wait, wait!

546
00:44:22,893 --> 00:44:24,762
Wait, you're too fast!

547
00:44:33,637 --> 00:44:36,840
There has been a sudden development
in the kidnappings in Setagaya.

548
00:44:36,907 --> 00:44:40,511
Four children were taken in total.

549
00:44:40,577 --> 00:44:43,714
It has been confirmed that one
third-grade girl who went missing has died

550
00:44:43,781 --> 00:44:44,882
in a warehouse.

551
00:44:44,948 --> 00:44:46,950
The arrested suspect is the unemployed

552
00:44:47,017 --> 00:44:49,486
Satoru Hatano.

553
00:44:49,553 --> 00:44:51,889
MIZUKI SAGARA

554
00:44:58,462 --> 00:45:03,400
‎NEXT TIME…

555
00:45:07,971 --> 00:45:08,906
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman
